[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Notable C behaviours confirmed preserved (not "fixed")
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Trailing garbage is **accepted**: `parse_val` only tests `endp != str`, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `"12abc"` parses as `12`. (`CONFIGS.md` row 13.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `"0x1f"` under base 10 parses as `0` and is accepted. (Row 14.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `"3000000000"` and `"-3000000000"` are rejected by the explicit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` range test with `errno == 0`, whereas
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `"99999999999999999999"` is rejected earlier by `errno == ERANGE`. Both print
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the same message but leave a **different** `errno`, and both are asserted.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`ERRORS.md` rows 2–5.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `int` overflow of `floors`/`bedrooms` wraps two's-complement; Rust uses
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `wrapping_add` and must not panic. (`ERRORS.md` rows 12–13.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `run` has external linkage despite not appearing in `driver.h`, so it is part
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   of the ABI and is exercised directly, not only through `driver`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `driver(NULL)` is unchecked in the C and faults inside `strtol`. Verified in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   forked children: **both** libraries die with `SIGSEGV` (signal 11).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`ERRORS.md` row 7.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `the_house` is never reset; consecutive calls keep accumulating.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`CONFIGS.md` row 21.)
